# Phase 13 Stage B pilot. NOT the confirmatory campaign, and decides no
# criterion: its seeds (13901..13908) are disjoint from every confirmatory
# range used or planned, and nothing measured here may be read against a
# C13 bar (ADR-0022 A7; the staged discipline is methodology review 6.1 as
# recorded in ADR-0029's campaign notes).
#
# What this pilot exists to lock, before the confirmatory document is
# written:
#
#   1. Wall-clock per world at the Phase 12 population tier with the
#      social section on. The Phase 13 benchmark measured the sense scan
#      at +41-45% of tick at 750 organisms with nothing bound
#      (experiments/results/phase13-benchmark-measurements.txt); these
#      worlds reach ~2,000 organisms, and whether 30 seeds x 7 arms x
#      60,000 ticks is affordable is a measurement, not an estimate
#      (D-121: campaign worlds are single-threaded by rule).
#   2. Naive-cohort sizes per relocation window, from `lifesim social
#      --epoch N` over the pilot manifest: C13.1's power depends on how
#      many naive individuals a 2,000-tick window actually produces, and
#      D-106's lesson is that a pre-registered N without a measured
#      per-world cohort size is a guess wearing a number.
#   3. Reachability drift: whether binding mutation at the Phase 12 rate
#      (binding_q16 16384) puts any hearers/speakers/rule-5 carriers in
#      the population within 60,000 ticks. A confirmatory C13.1 null with
#      zero social bindings everywhere is a reachability null, and if the
#      pilot already shows empty censuses the confirmatory must either
#      raise the horizon or say up front what its null can and cannot
#      mean (D-117 against D-099).
#   4. Which relocation epochs are analyzable: cohort and census both, so
#      the confirmatory can name its epochs in advance instead of
#      choosing them after seeing data.
#
# Environment: the Phase 12 confirmatory base carried unchanged, plus the
# Phase 11 relocating patch (interval 2,000, radius 32, capacity scale
# 4x - the variable environment C11.1 used, which is what gives C13.1 its
# patch P and its arrival clock), plus the Phase 11 plasticity block with
# the chain gate ON (`plasticity.live_rule_zero true`, citing D-120: the
# chain meets its reachability bar 10/12 and the moat fails 4/12), plus
# the social section. Arms A and C only - the primary C13.1 contrast; the
# full B/D/S ladder belongs to the confirmatory. C differs from A in
# exactly its named variables (perception_enabled, signal_enabled), the
# D-118 lesson applied in advance: both arms carry observational_enabled
# so the gate itself is common-mode, and with perception off rule 5's cue
# reads zero through the mechanism's own path rather than through a
# second flag.
#
# Outputs mirror what the confirmatory will write (events, snapshots,
# spatial 50 for the arrival series, actions 500 for the fidelity work),
# so the pilot's wall-clock includes the instrumentation it is sizing.

campaign phase13-social-pilot
ticks 60000
workers 8
seeds 13901..13908
base preset phase2
base cells_x 128
base cells_y 128
base initial_organisms 200
base max_entities 40000
base cell_capacity_milli 240000
base genome2.enabled true
base physiology.enabled true
base physiology.extrinsic_hazard_q16_per_s 13
base genome2.mutation.point_q16 65535
base genome2.mutation.point_delta_q16 3277
base genome2.mutation.duplication_q16 6554
base genome2.mutation.deletion_q16 655
base genome2.mutation.insertion_q16 0
base genome2.mutation.transposition_q16 0
base genome2.mutation.max_run 3
base genome2.mutation.binding_q16 16384
base genome2.mutation.plasticity_enabled true
base genome2.caps.max_loci_per_chromosome 160
base genome2.caps.max_nodes 160
base genome2.caps.max_edges 160
base genome2.caps.max_edges_per_node 32
base genome2.caps.max_genome_bytes 16384
base contest.enabled true
base probe.enabled true
base probe.action_census_enabled true
base probe.marker_locus_enabled true
base plasticity.enabled true
base plasticity.max_plastic_edges 32
base plasticity.plastic_edge_cost_milli_per_s 2
base plasticity.lamarckian_fraction_q16 0
base plasticity.live_rule_zero true
base worldmod.enabled true
base worldmod.patch_enabled true
base worldmod.relocate_interval_ticks 2000
base worldmod.patch_radius_cells 32
base worldmod.patch_capacity_scale_q16 262144
base worldmod.max_capacity_overrides 8192
base worldmod.max_material_overrides 8192
base artifact.enabled true
base artifact.max_objects 4096
base artifact.max_objects_per_cell 8
base artifact.max_composition_depth 4
base artifact.max_composition_breadth 8
base artifact.max_held_objects 1
base artifact.max_candidates 8
base artifact.carry_capacity_milli 4000
base artifact.carry_move_cost_q16 65536
base artifact.hold_cost_milli_per_s 20
base artifact.action_cost_milli 60
base artifact.strike_cost_milli 120
base artifact.action_threshold_q16 32768
base artifact.reach_m 2
base artifact.consume_reach_m 2
base artifact.perception_range_m 8
base artifact.strike_force_q16 262144
base artifact.strike_mass_reference_milli 2000
base artifact.fracture_margin_q16 65536
base artifact.max_fragments 4
base artifact.min_fragment_mass_milli 100
base artifact.joint_floor_q16 16384
base artifact.blocking_mass_milli 3000
base artifact.terrain_yield_milli 6000
base artifact.extraction_milli 800
base artifact.yield_regen_milli 400
base artifact.yield_regen_interval_ticks 600
base artifact.stone_relative_q16 39322
base artifact.wood_relative_q16 16384
base social.enabled true
base social.observational_enabled true
condition A
condition C
set A social.perception_enabled true
set A social.signal_enabled true
set C social.perception_enabled false
set C social.signal_enabled false
vary social.perception_enabled
vary social.signal_enabled
output events on
output snapshots on
output actions 500
output spatial 50
